      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "We need to find \\(\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)\\) given that \\(\\tan x = 2\\).\n\nWe will use the tangent addition formula:\n\\[\n\\tan(a + b) = \\frac{\\tan a + \\tan b}{1 - \\tan a \\tan b}\n\\]\nIn our case, \\(a = x\\) and \\(b = \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\). So, we have:\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}\n\\]\n\nWe know that \\(\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1\\). Therefore, we can substitute \\(\\tan x = 2\\) into the formula:\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{3}{1 - 2} = \\frac{3}{-1} = -3\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)\\) is \\(\\boxed{-3}\\).",
