      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find \\(\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)\\) given that \\(\\tan x = 2\\), we use the tangent addition formula, which states:\n\\[\n\\tan (A + B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}\n\\]\nIn this problem, \\(A = x\\) and \\(B = \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\). We know that \\(\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1\\). Substituting these values into the formula, we get:\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}\n\\]\nSubstituting \\(\\tan x = 2\\) and \\(\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1\\) into the equation, we have:\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{3}{1 - 2} = \\frac{3}{-1} = -3\n\\]\nThus, the value of \\(\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)\\) is \\(\\boxed{-3}\\).",
